@startuml fig2b_functional_units
' Diagram 2b of the IEC 60050-351 pattern: the functional units of Figures 1
' and 2 of the standard.
'
' Conventions: shared/FIGURES.md. Flat boxes, no namespace prefixes, no clause
' numbers, orthogonal edges, nothing explanatory inside the drawing.
'
' What it shows: which functional units the standard names, and the two
' relations that hold between them, composition and the membership of the final
' controlling element in the controlled system.
'
' The sensing element and the measuring element stand apart on purpose. They
' are separate entries, 351-56-26 and 351-49-05, and the standard states no
' composition between them, so none is drawn. The measuring transmitter,
' 351-56-29, is the unit whose output is a standardised signal, which is where
' the communication subdomain begins.
'
' Left out on purpose:
'  - how a unit is reached by an action line, and how it is realised by
'    hardware: diagram 2
'  - the kinds of control: diagram 1
'
' Split off from diagram 2 because twelve subclasses on one node crowd out the
' mechanism that diagram is about.

skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 22
skinparam ranksep 42
skinparam padding 3
skinparam ArrowColor #1A2733
skinparam ArrowFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowFontColor #1A2733
hide empty members
hide circle
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FCEFC7
  BorderColor #C9A227
  FontColor #1A2733
  FontSize 14
  BorderThickness 1
}

class FunctionalUnit

' --- the systems ----------------------------------------------------
class ControlSystem
class ControllingSystem
class ControlledSystem

' --- the elements of the forward branch ------------------------------
class ReferenceVariableGeneratingElement
class ComparingElement
class ControllingElement
class Controller

' --- the manipulating side -------------------------------------------
class FinalControllingEquipment
class Actuator
class FinalControllingElement

' --- the measuring side ----------------------------------------------
class MeasuringElement
class SensingElement
class MeasuringTransmitter

FunctionalUnit <|-- ControlSystem
FunctionalUnit <|-- ControllingSystem
FunctionalUnit <|-- ControlledSystem
FunctionalUnit <|-- ReferenceVariableGeneratingElement
FunctionalUnit <|-- ComparingElement
FunctionalUnit <|-- ControllingElement
FunctionalUnit <|-- Controller
FunctionalUnit <|-- FinalControllingEquipment
FunctionalUnit <|-- Actuator
FunctionalUnit <|-- FinalControllingElement
FunctionalUnit <|-- MeasuringElement
FunctionalUnit <|-- SensingElement
FunctionalUnit <|-- MeasuringTransmitter

' --- what the standard composes from what -----------------------------
ControlSystem              --> ControllingSystem       : consistsOfUnit
ControlSystem              --> ControlledSystem        : consistsOfUnit
Controller                 --> ComparingElement        : consistsOfUnit
Controller                 --> ControllingElement      : consistsOfUnit
FinalControllingEquipment  --> Actuator                : consistsOfUnit
FinalControllingEquipment  --> FinalControllingElement : consistsOfUnit

' --- the membership the standard states explicitly --------------------
FinalControllingElement --> "1" ControlledSystem : partOfControlledSystem

@enduml
